  "notes": "REGISTER:\nPolite and formal (お + {詫|わ}び, from ⟦{詫|わ}びる→詫びる：14174_wabiru⟧). Standard in business and public apologies; in casual speech people say ごめん or すみません instead.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- お{詫|わ}び⟦{申|もう}し{上|あ}げます→申し上げる：01734_moushiageru⟧ (I humbly apologize; very formal)\n- お{詫|わ}びいたします (I apologize; formal)\n- お{詫|わ}びの⟦{言葉|ことば}→言葉：02880_kotoba⟧ (words of apology)\n- お{詫|わ}びの⟦{品|しな}→品：03192_shina⟧/⟦{印|しるし}→印：03254_shirushi⟧ (a gift offered as an apology)\n- お{詫|わ}び⟦{状|じょう}→状：09878_jou⟧ (letter of apology)\n- お{詫|わ}びとお⟦{知|し}らせ→知らせ：03252_shirase⟧ (notice of apology, e.g. for an error on a website)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{謝罪|しゃざい}→謝罪：06754_shazai⟧: apology as an act, more formal and often public ({謝罪会見|しゃざいかいけん}); not used in the humble set phrases above\n- ⟦{陳謝|ちんしゃ}→陳謝：07994_chinsha⟧: a formal apology, mostly in news writing\n- ごめんなさい / すみません: everyday spoken apologies\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{詫|わ}びる→詫びる：14174_wabiru⟧ (to apologize)\n- ⟦{謝|あやま}る→謝る：01177_ayamaru⟧ (to apologize; the everyday verb)",
